{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-87555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $5$ data points, where \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}=-20,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2}=170.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}=-20,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-20) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2}=170,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 170 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =34-{(-4)}^{2} \\\\  & =34-16 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0547da550ceeca3be7892e54138ea8b21a3205165531361b6fdbdd4e9c71f512"} {"question" "q-87555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $7$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=201.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=35,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 35 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=201,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 201 \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}-{(5)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{201}{7}-25 \\\\  & =\\frac{201-175}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0547da550ceeca3be7892e54138ea8b21a3205165531361b6fdbdd4e9c71f512"} {"question" "q-87564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{201}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{22}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{26}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{46}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{97}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-87564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{26}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n-18,\\,-11,\\,-8,\\,4,\\,6,\\,-3\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-18-11-8+4+6-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-30) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot ((-18)^{2}+(-11)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (324+121+64+16+36+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 570 \\\\  & =\\frac{570}{6} \\\\  & =95.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =95-{(-5)}^{2} \\\\  & =95-25 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0547da550ceeca3be7892e54138ea8b21a3205165531361b6fdbdd4e9c71f512"} {"question" "q-263422" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263422" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "70"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n10,\\,14,\\,16,\\,9,\\,12,\\,5\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (10+14+16+9+12+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 66 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot [{10}^{2}+{14}^{2}+{16}^{2}+{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}+{5}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot [100+196+256+81+144+25] \\\\  & =\\frac{802}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}-{(11)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{401}{3}-121 \\\\  & =\\frac{401-363}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{38}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0547da550ceeca3be7892e54138ea8b21a3205165531361b6fdbdd4e9c71f512"} {"question" "q-263451" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263451" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{38}{3}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n9,\\,4,\\,15,\\,14,\\,18,\\,7,\\,17\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (9+4+15+14+18+7+17) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 84 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [{9}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{15}^{2}+{14}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{17}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [81+16+225+196+324+49+289] \\\\  & =\\frac{1180}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1180}{7}-{(12)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1180}{7}-144 \\\\  & =\\frac{1180-1008}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{172}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{172}{7}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{43}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0547da550ceeca3be7892e54138ea8b21a3205165531361b6fdbdd4e9c71f512"} {"question" "q-263584" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"} {"question" "q-263584" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{172}{7}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069126/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5466a11015fde21fb894261ab2ec8e84c32535a5bcfd41cc47d133631fd02b3"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2343 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
